# Whether a derivation covers the artifact, or one site of it.
#
# Every other line this tool prints is about a step: which rule applied
# where, at what cost, resting on which obligations. None of them says
# the thing a consumer is actually after — that the artifact as a whole
# is discharged — and `soundness.md` §8.1 already claims a third party
# re-checks *the derivation*, which is a claim about a final sequent the
# system did not produce.
#
# The judgment is not a new check. Seal decided the policy and refused
# an escaping claim, and the claim graph is already in the sealed view.
# What is new is saying that they hold together with a derivation's own
# coverage. That is an accounting statement over an artifact rather than
# a security theorem about a subject, which is why it is computed here
# and not written as a signature rule: the rule language would have
# needed a notion, a body kind, an artifact projection, and a view field
# to say something it is not for.

# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t

# A closed proof: one conclusion, nothing left standing, sealed under
# the policy that admits no residual.
# RUN: zkc-seal %S/../Encoding/routed-schnorr.mlir %zkc-seal-full -o %t/closed.artifacts > /dev/null
# RUN: %python %S/../SemanticClosure/lib/artifact_handoff.py stage %t/closed.artifacts %t/closed.mlirbc
# RUN: zkc-derive --signature=%zkc-registry-dir/soundness-signature.json \
# RUN:   --protocol-vocabulary=%zkc-registry-dir/protocol-vocabulary.json \
# RUN:   --construction-profile-registry=%zkc-registry-dir/construction-profiles.json \
# RUN:   --request=%S/Inputs/schnorr-completeness-request.json -o=%t/w.json \
# RUN:   %t/closed.mlirbc | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=CLOSED
# CLOSED: artifact judgment: discharged (policy closed_proof)

# An artifact sealed for analysis says so. This is not a defect and the
# judgment does not treat it as one: an `analysis_only_artifact` never
# claimed to be a closed proof, and reporting the policy is what lets a
# reader tell "this derivation is incomplete" from "this artifact does
# not claim closure".
# RUN: zkc-seal %S/Inputs/r1cs-entry.mlir %zkc-seal-full -o %t/analysis.artifacts > /dev/null
# RUN: %python %S/../SemanticClosure/lib/artifact_handoff.py stage %t/analysis.artifacts %t/analysis.mlirbc
# RUN: zkc-derive --signature=%zkc-registry-dir/soundness-signature.json \
# RUN:   --protocol-vocabulary=%zkc-registry-dir/protocol-vocabulary.json \
# RUN:   --construction-profile-registry=%zkc-registry-dir/construction-profiles.json \
# RUN:   --request=%S/Inputs/r1cs-entry-request.json -o=%t/w2.json \
# RUN:   %t/analysis.mlirbc | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ANALYSIS
# ANALYSIS: artifact judgment: not discharged (policy analysis_only_artifact)
